## The finding

`dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-storytime-book-cover.ts` resolved `--out` but did not reject a path inside `proof/` or `proof-v2/`. The writes use fixed names, so a `--version 3` build with `--out` in `proof/` overwrote the version 1 mocks. The versioned default folder protected only a build that took the default. This broke FR-5.7 and mutant M22.

## Precondition note

The range `phase_base_sha..HEAD` holds no committed Red test for B-P1-01. A grep for `R29` and `checkStorytimeCoverOutDir` found no hit in the track files, and the last commit of the cover test file is 2d6b503e (D11.5). The orchestrator handoff gave the R29 test cases in step 4 and scoped them into this Green task. Green therefore added the R29 tests together with the fix, in commit 3f5c42a1. The targeted Red command was rerun first: it passed with 43 tests, because no test measured this behavior. The three mutants are the proof that the new tests fail without the fix.

## The change (commit 3f5c42a1)

- `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/covers.ts`: new export `checkStorytimeCoverOutDir(out, version, printReadyRoot): string[]`. It resolves `out` through the deepest existing ancestor with `fs.realpathSync` and joins the rest of the path. It lists the existing version folders under `<printReadyRoot>/storytime/` (`proof` is version 1, `proof-v<k>` is version k), takes the real path of each folder of another version, and returns an error when the resolved `out` equals it or is inside it. The error names the folder and its version. When `out` exists, it returns an error for each of `front.png`, `back.png`, `cover.pdf`, `corner-mode.txt`, and `build-report.json` that is a symbolic link.
- `dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-storytime-book-cover.ts`: one `printReadyRoot` constant, used by the default folder and by the check. The check runs right after the `--version` check, before the data load and any write. Each error prints to stderr and the script returns 2.
- `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-covers-16books.test.ts`: R29 helper cases (version 3 into `proof/l2u1`, into `proof-v2/l2u1`, and through a symbolic link to `proof`; version 3 into `proof-v3/l2u1` gives `[]`; version 1 into `proof` and version 2 into `proof-v2` give `[]`; a `front.png` symbolic link in the output folder gives an error). One R29 CLI case runs with `HOME` in a temp root, a seed `front.png`, and expects exit 2 with the seed bytes unchanged. `runScript` gained an optional env argument. No test points at the real `~/Desktop/print-ready`; every root comes from `mkdtempSync`.
- Plan row: new `[~]` task, then `[x]` in commit 5f8b26f9.
- `measure/lessons-learned.md`: one durable line under Recurring Gotchas.

